sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-04> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Horns of wild goats and sheep form a series of homologous logarithmic spirals with increasing constant angle: under 40° in Oryx, under 70° in the Scinde wild goat, about 75° in Ovis ammon and a little more in the Highland ram.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Goat and sheep horns form a series of homologous spirals of increasing angle";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "\\alpha < 40^\\circ (Oryx), < 70^\\circ (Scinde wild goat), \\approx 75^\\circ (Ovis ammon), > 75^\\circ (Highland ram)";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XIII, “The Shapes of Horns, and of Teeth or Tusks: with a Note on Torsion”; topic “Spiral angle of horns”. Scope: horns of Oryx, Capra and Ovis species"
}
